# KNOWN GAP — SELF-HOST LANE. `Dict[String, int].contains_key(...)` does not
# LINK on any self-host driver. Rust gg compiles and runs it correctly.
#
# This is a lane divergence with a known direction: Rust is right, the
# self-host lags, so the self-host is what gets fixed (never dumb the Rust
# side down to match -- and never reshape fixtures to avoid the gap, which is
# how a workaround idiom becomes load-bearing).
#
# Rust lane, orchestrator-verified 2026-08-24: prints HAS / 1.
# Self-host lane: link failure on all drivers (R44 Track-K pass-10 measurement).
#
# ⚠ WHY THIS IS FILED RATHER THAN WORKED AROUND: an earlier decision in the R44
# Track-K brief turned this into a fixture-authoring workaround ("use v[key]
# instead"), which buries the bug exactly the way the playbook forbids. The
# workaround may still be used where a fixture's SUBJECT is something else, but
# the gap itself is recorded here with a repro.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints HAS then 1 on every lane.

from std.collections import Dict

void main():
    Dict[String, int] d = {}
    d.put("k0", 7)
    if d.contains_key("k0"):
        print("HAS")
    else:
        print("MISS")
    print(d.len())
